<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Drone platforms (D'thorga Patches 0.22.0; docs/development/top-up-design.md; owner, 18 Nov 2026: colonists never refilled The Dead
    Man's Switch's engineering drone bays with steel). Fortified Features Framework's platform comp holds the store and offers only a
    right-click "fill" order; this names the comp, so D'thorga Framework's haulers top it up to the level that order fills it to (the platform's starting store, which the player cannot change). Every
    building with the comp is covered (the engineering drone bay, the trashpan and hound stations and the FPV nest), and since D'thorga
    Framework 0.135.0 every mechanoid with it too (the Hermit Crab and the Cluster Weaver), by a mechanitor, as mech repair is. The least load is
    the platform's own cost of one drone, so a hauler walks once a drone's worth is missing.

    The three names are members of Fortified.CompMechPlatform as read on 18 Nov 2026 (the build of 12 Nov 2026): AmountToAutofill (its
    target less what it holds), Props.fixedIngredient and CostPerPawn. Loaded only with Fortified Features Framework. An addition, not
    a fix of a fault; docs/development/temporary-patches.md notes it under "Left out on purpose", with how to retire it. Not yet tested in game.
  -->
  <Phobos.Framework.TopUp.PhobosTopUpDef>
    <defName>PhobosTopUp_FortifiedMechPlatform</defName>
    <label>drone platform</label>
    <compClass>Fortified.CompMechPlatform</compClass>
    <wantedMember>AmountToAutofill</wantedMember>
    <ingredientMember>Props.fixedIngredient</ingredientMember>
    <leastLoadMember>CostPerPawn</leastLoadMember>
  </Phobos.Framework.TopUp.PhobosTopUpDef>
</Defs>
